{"seq":35,"slug":"type-checking-semantic-analysis","title":"类型检查与语义分析","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 类型检查与语义分析\n\n解析器把源代码变成一棵语法正确的抽象语法树，但语法正确远不等于程序有意义。一个变量在使用前是否声明过，一个函数调用的实参类型能否匹配形参，一个 `return` 是否出现在函数体内——这些问题语法分析无力回答，它们属于语义分析的领地。类型检查与语义分析处在编译器的中端：上游是前端的词法与语法分析，下游是后端的优化与代码生成。它既是程序正确性的最后一道静态防线，也是把「人写的源语言」翻译成「机器可优化的中间表示」的语义桥梁。\n\n这个 hub 按四章组织，刻意安排成层层递进的认知路径。第一章「基础」回答「语义分析在做什么、靠什么数据结构做」：先有阶段总览看清它在编译管线中的位置，再深入符号表与作用域这一切语义查询的基石，最后落到名称解析——把每一处标识符引用绑定到它的声明。没有名称绑定，类型检查连「这个变量是什么类型」都无从谈起，所以基础章是后续一切的前提。\n\n第二章「类型检查」是 hub 的理论核心。它从类型规则与判断出发，用形式化的推理规则 $\\Gamma \\vdash e : \\tau$ 精确定义「什么样的程序是良类型的」；接着讲类型推断，即在程序员不写注解时算法如何自动推出类型，Hindley-Milner 与 Algorithm W 在此安家；最后是子类型与隐式转换，处理「一个类型能否当作另一个类型用」这一现实语言绕不开的灵活性。这三篇构成「规则—推断—关系」的完整闭环。\n\n第三章「高级类型」把检查能力推向工业语言真正需要的表达力：泛型与多态让一段代码服务于多种类型，流敏感类型让同一变量在不同控制流分支里拥有更精确的类型，效果与所有权检查则把类型系统的疆界从「值是什么」拓展到「计算做了什么、谁拥有这块内存」——Rust 的借用检查器是其最著名的实践。第四章「实践」回到工程现场：如何把类型错误报得让人看得懂、如何用渐进与双向类型检查在动态与静态之间取得平衡、以及如何把通过检查的语义信息下降为带类型的中间表示交给后端。\n\n读完四章，你会看到一条清晰的主线：从「绑定名字」到「判定类型」，从「单一类型」到「精确而富表达力的类型」，最终把这一切凝结成可供代码生成消费的语义产物。这正是现代编译器中端的完整故事。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"semantic-analysis-overview","title":"语义分析阶段总览","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/foundations/semantic-analysis-overview"},{"seq":2,"slug":"symbol-tables-scoping","title":"符号表与作用域解析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/foundations/symbol-tables-scoping"},{"seq":3,"slug":"name-resolution","title":"名称解析与绑定","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/foundations/name-resolution"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"type-checking","title":"类型检查","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/type-checking","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"type-rules-judgments","title":"类型规则与判断","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/type-checking/type-rules-judgments"},{"seq":2,"slug":"type-inference","title":"类型推断","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/type-checking/type-inference"},{"seq":3,"slug":"subtyping-coercion","title":"子类型与隐式转换","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/type-checking/subtyping-coercion"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"advanced-typing","title":"高级类型","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/advanced-typing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"generics-polymorphism","title":"泛型与多态检查","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/advanced-typing/generics-polymorphism"},{"seq":2,"slug":"flow-sensitive-typing","title":"流敏感类型与细化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/advanced-typing/flow-sensitive-typing"},{"seq":3,"slug":"effect-ownership-checks","title":"效果与所有权检查","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/advanced-typing/effect-ownership-checks"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"error-reporting","title":"类型错误诊断","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/practice/error-reporting"},{"seq":2,"slug":"gradual-bidirectional","title":"渐进与双向类型检查","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/practice/gradual-bidirectional"},{"seq":3,"slug":"semantic-ir-lowering","title":"语义检查到 IR 的下降","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/type-checking-semantic-analysis/practice/semantic-ir-lowering"}]}]}